{"name":"Pink Peacock","hex":"#d3236f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"peacock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male peafowl, especially Pavo cristatus, notable for its brilliant iridescently ocellated tail.","A peafowl (of the genus Pavo or Afropavo), either male or female."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strut about proudly or haughtily.","To engage in peacocking, ostentatious dress or behaviour to impress women."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peacock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pink Peacock","blocks":[{"text":"Pink Peacock was a café and infoshop in the Govanhill area of Glasgow, Scotland. Described by its founders as \"anti-Zionist\" and \"the only queer Yiddish anarchist vegan pay-what-you-can café in the world\", it opened physically in 2021, after being delayed by the COVID-19 pandemic, and announced its closure in June 2023."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/PinkPeacockLogo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Peacock","wikidata":"Q111328096"},{"title":"Peafowl","blocks":[{"text":"Peafowl is a common name for two bird species of the genus Pavo and one species of the closely related genus Afropavo within the tribe Pavonini of the family Phasianidae. Male peafowl are referred to as peacocks, and female peafowl are referred to as peahens. Despite this, peacock is usually used to refer to both sexes, in common language."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Peacock_Plumage.jpg/330px-Peacock_Plumage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peafowl","wikidata":"Q201251"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Pink_Peacock_storefront.jpg/500px-Pink_Peacock_storefront.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Pink_Peacock_storefront.jpg/1280px-Pink_Peacock_storefront.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Pink_Peacock_storefront.jpg/500px-Pink_Peacock_storefront.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_Peacock_storefront.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Pink_Peacock_interior.jpg/500px-Pink_Peacock_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Pink_Peacock_interior.jpg/1280px-Pink_Peacock_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Pink_Peacock_interior.jpg/500px-Pink_Peacock_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Café interior in November 2021","link":"htt